From 0432351a714fb1262b506803d6299f0f9ae9aa4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:19:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] Add a save writer for editing the save of a batteryless
 repro cart

extract_save.py copies the 128 KiB save out of a ROM dump for PKHeX.
make_save_writer.py builds a multiboot program from a dump and an edited
save; sent over the link cable, it writes the save into the cart's save
area in ROM flash, with the flasher's checks: identity against the dump,
the board probe, CFI block size checked by a test erase in unused space,
and L+R+A before writing. The image carries the whole save, so a rerun
after a power cut finishes the write. The screen shows the trainer name,
ID and play time of the save on the cart and of the new one.

The flasher's binary is unchanged; its area planning moved into
plan_areas() so both builders choose the same unused areas.
savewriter_emu_test.py runs the save writer on every simulated board,
with power cuts, failures, a cart already flashed and refusals.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
